            "type": "reasoning",
            "content": [
              {
                "text": "I'm noticing the color assignments seem odd across examples\u2014single cells vanishing, pairs getting different colors than expected. Maybe the coloring depends on order of appearance rather than shape size, so I want to trace through example 1's shapes to test that theory.\n\nTesting columns as the key: in example 1, columns 1,2,4,8 map to colors 1,2,3,4 respectively \u2014 that's just their rank order among columns. Checking example 2, columns with 0s ranked 0,1,3,4,6,7,8 map to 1,2,3,4,5,6,7, and it matches except column 6 which would be color 5 (the background color, so it's invisible). So the rule seems to be: color equals the rank of that column among all columns containing 0s.",
                "type": "reasoning_text"
              }
            ],
